Default — stdio transport, system netstead <p>The simplest config: relies on <code>netstead</code> being on the MCP host’s <code>PATH</code>.</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "netstead": { "command": "netstead", "args": ["mcp", "serve"] }
  }
}
</code></pre> Rename the server in the host UI <p><code>--name</code> becomes the label under the tool list in Claude.</p> <pre><code>"args": ["mcp", "serve", "--name", "gmns-leavenworth"]
</code></pre> Run inside a project venv <p>Use the absolute path to that venv’s <code>netstead</code> binary; avoids version skew with the system install.</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "netstead": {
      "command": "/path/to/.venv/bin/netstead",
      "args": ["mcp", "serve"]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> Pin the server to a working directory <p>Adds <code>cwd</code> so all relative-path tool calls resolve from a known root.</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "netstead": {
      "command": "netstead",
      "args": ["mcp", "serve"],
      "cwd": "/abs/path/to/data"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> Pass env vars (cloud creds) <p>Use <code>env</code> to inject credentials into the subprocess.</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "netstead": {
      "command": "netstead",
      "args": ["mcp", "serve"],
      "env": { "AWS_PROFILE": "ds-readonly" }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
